#
# WLCS tests fluxland is known to fail, each with its reason:
# tools/ci.sh wlcs skips them (a gtest negative filter), so any other
# failure fails CI. Regenerate after a WLCS upgrade; a fixed one should
# come off the list.

# WLCS's own expectations of the compositor that the protocol doesn't make,
# or that wlroots meets differently. Each is checked against WLCS 1.7.0's
# source (Debian trixie's package); Mir's own list of WLCS failures
# (tests/acceptance-tests/wayland/expected_wlcs_failures.list in
# canonical/mir) has several of them too.

# xdg_surface_stable.cpp: the error is expected at attach; wlroots raises
# it at the commit, where xdg-shell checks it (on Mir's list too).
XdgSurfaceStableTest.attaching_buffer_to_unconfigured_xdg_surface_is_an_error
